			"date": "2025-04-28T18:07:53.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I need to build a website with a lot of pages (thousands). I do not want to rebuild the entire site each time an update is needed on 1 page (regularly 1 or few pages will need an update). So the plans were to **start** with 11ty, keep a limited compatibility for site wide changes and dev a solution that allow to make edits from a dedicated app that can produce the same output. <br>11ty running in the browser will remove or simplify some of the challenges.</p>",
